			"color":"#9a7628",
			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the young woman in <Picture 1>, with her appearance, facial features, hairstyle, clothing, and seated driving posture preserved as the main visible subject of the target video.\n<Subject 2> is the in-car environment shown in <Picture 1>, including the vehicle interior, driver's seat position, dashboard area, and realistic driving setting.\n<Audio 1> is the voice-timbre reference for <Subject 1> (S1), providing the female speaker's vocal characteristics, tone, emotional expression, speaking pace, and delivery style for synchronized dialogue performance.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reference] The target video shows <Subject 1> driving a car while making a phone call inside <Subject 2>. The woman's facial expression is extremely anxious and panicked, with accurate lip synchronization matching the speech generated from <Audio 1>. <Audio 1> is used as a voice-timbre and emotional delivery reference for <Subject 1> (S1), creating a similar female voice performance without directly copying the original audio signal.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the woman's identity, appearance, driving posture, anxious facial expression, and visible emotional state are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1], [Shot 2], [Shot 3]): fully_preserved - the car interior environment, driver's seat composition, dashboard elements, and enclosed driving atmosphere are retained.\n<Picture 1> (visual reference for [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the image composition, woman placement, and in-car scene arrangement are used as the visual foundation for the target video.\n<Audio 1>: reference - its female voice timbre, emotional intensity, speaking rhythm, and delivery style guide <Subject 1> (S1)'s generated speech without directly copying the original audio signal.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic cinematic close-up scene inside a moving car, with natural daylight entering through the windows and a tense emotional atmosphere. The camera maintains a documentary-style handheld feeling while focusing on the driver's face, mouth movement, and emotional reaction.\n\n[Shot 1] The shot begins from <Picture 1>, showing <Subject 2>, the interior of a car with the driver seated behind the steering wheel. <Subject 1>, the young woman with the preserved appearance from <Picture 1>, is driving while holding a phone near her ear. Her eyes are wide, eyebrows are raised, and her expression is visibly frightened and nervous. She looks between the road ahead and the phone, breathing tensely while her lips move naturally in sync with the generated speech. <Subject 1> (S1) speaks with the female voice characteristics, anxious tone, emotional intensity, and speaking pace referenced from <Audio 1>, saying, <d>[Chinese] [generated synchronized speech matching the reference audio]</d>.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:05.000, the camera moves into a tighter close-up on <Subject 1>'s face and upper body. The phone remains beside her ear, and the steering wheel edge is visible in the foreground. Her worried expression becomes stronger as she frowns slightly, swallows nervously, and glances toward the road. Her mouth movements remain precisely synchronized with <Subject 1> (S1)'s spoken audio. The voice continues with the same female timbre, anxious emotion, and measured but urgent delivery style referenced from <Audio 1>.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:10.000, the camera shifts slightly to a side angle, revealing more of <Subject 2> and the woman's driving position. <Subject 1> grips the steering wheel more tightly while continuing the phone conversation. Her facial expression remains panicked and tense, and the final spoken phrase ends with matching lip movement and emotional delivery. The shot concludes with her still focused on the road, maintaining the anxious atmosphere.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nRealistic car interior ambience continues throughout the video, including soft engine noise, road movement sounds, subtle vehicle vibration, and faint phone-call audio presence. No copied audio signal from <Audio 1> is used directly; only the voice characteristics are referenced.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
